---
title: Invoices
description: Create invoices, print them with a Swiss QR-bill and follow them until they're paid.
---

## Before your first invoice

Have a look at **Settings → Billing**. Three defaults save you typing on every invoice:

- **Payment term (days)**: sets the due date. 30 days unless you change it.
- **Default VAT rate**: preselected on new invoices.
- **Default bank account**: the account printed on your QR-bills and used when recording payments.

For QR-bills, you also need a [bank account](/en/banking/bank-accounts/) and your organization's full address under **Settings → Details**.

## Create an invoice

{% steps %}

1. Go to **Billing → Invoices** and choose **Create an invoice**.

2. Pick the **Client** and check the **Issue date** and **Due date**.

3. Pick the **VAT rate**. It applies to the whole invoice.

4. Pick the **Currency**. For a foreign currency, enter the **Exchange rate**.

5. Add the lines with **Add a line**: a **Description**, a **Quantity** and a **Unit price**. Use the **Discount** type for a line that's taken off the total.

{% /steps %}

The new invoice is a **Draft**. You can still add and remove lines, or delete it altogether.

## Open it

When it's ready, choose **Open**. nullish gives the invoice its number, books it in your journal and generates its payment reference. From then on its lines can't change.

{% aside %}
Invoice numbers count up per client. Payment references are random, so they don't reveal how many
invoices you send.
{% /aside %}

## Print it

Choose **PDF**, pick the **Document template**, the **Language** and the **Bank account**, then **Generate PDF**. A few seconds later, **Download** it.

The PDF includes a Swiss QR-bill when a bank account is selected and the invoice is in CHF or EUR. Drafts print with a "Draft" watermark and no QR-bill, handy for a last check.

nullish doesn't send emails: download the PDF and send it the way you usually do.

## Get paid

The easiest way is to [import your bank statements](/en/banking/import-statements/): nullish recognizes payments by their reference and suggests the matching invoice.

You can also record a payment by hand: choose **Pay**, then enter the **Date**, the **Bank account** and the **Amount**.

Either way:

- A partial payment leaves the invoice **Open** with what remains due.
- Once everything's paid, the invoice becomes **Paid**.
- If a client pays too much, the difference is booked for you.

## When things go wrong

- **Void**: the invoice shouldn't exist, for example it was sent to the wrong client. Its bookings are reversed. Only possible before any payment.
- **Write off**: the client won't pay. The open amount is booked as a loss on receivables and the invoice becomes **Uncollectible**.

{% aside type="caution" %}Both are final. There's no undo.{% /aside %}

## Statuses

| Status        | Meaning                                   |
| ------------- | ----------------------------------------- |
| Draft         | Still being prepared. Nothing booked yet. |
| Open          | Booked and waiting for payment.           |
| Paid          | Fully paid.                               |
| Uncollectible | Written off.                              |
| Void          | Cancelled. Its bookings are reversed.     |
